      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is incredibly common to feel invisible and like a \"ghost\" in a new place, especially when the initial excitement of a life change sets in and is followed by the quiet struggle of finding a rhythm. Remember that your presence is vital to the people you know, even if it doesn't feel that way right now from the inside. Try to engage in just one small daily activity, like joining a local group or talking to a neighbor, to help you feel more grounded and seen. You are not taking up space you don't deserve; you are simply still finding your way in a new home.",
